  n1: Inputs.number([1.3, 1.7], {value: 1.4532, step: 0.0001, label: "core index n₁"}),
  n2: Inputs.number([1.3, 1.7], {value: 1.4485, step: 0.0001, label: "cladding index n₂"}),
  d:  Inputs.number([1, 1000], {value: 8.2, step: 0.1, label: "core diameter 2a (µm)"}),
  lam: Inputs.number([0.3, 2.5], {value: 1.31, step: 0.01, label: "wavelength λ (µm)"})
})









Show the Python
fiberOut = {
  const {n1, n2, d, lam} = fd, a = d / 2;
  if (!(n1 &gt; n2)) return null;
  const NAv = Math.sqrt(n1*n1 - n2*n2), Dl = (n1*n1 - n2*n2) / (2*n1*n1);
  const V = 2*Math.PI*a/lam*NAv, lc = 2*Math.PI*a*NAv/2.405;
  const mfd = 2*a*(0.65 + 1.619*Math.pow(V, -1.5) + 2.879*Math.pow(V, -6));
  return {NAv, Dl, V, lc, mfd, amax: Math.asin(Math.min(NAv, 1)) * 180/Math.PI, M: V*V/2,
          dtau: (n1 - n2) / 299792458 * 1e3 * 1e9};
}
fiberOut === null ? html`&lt;div class="result-box"&gt;n₁ must be larger than n₂.&lt;/div&gt;` :
html`&lt;div class="result-box"&gt;
Δ = ${(100*fiberOut.Dl).toFixed(3)} % · NA = ${fiberOut.NAv.toFixed(4)} ·
α&lt;sub&gt;max&lt;/sub&gt; = ${fiberOut.amax.toFixed(2)}° (total 2α&lt;sub&gt;max&lt;/sub&gt; = ${(2*fiberOut.amax).toFixed(1)}°)&lt;br&gt;
V = &lt;b&gt;${fiberOut.V.toFixed(3)}&lt;/b&gt; → ${fiberOut.V &lt; 2.405 ? "&lt;b&gt;single-mode&lt;/b&gt;" : `&lt;b&gt;multimode&lt;/b&gt;, M ≈ V²/2 ≈ ${Math.round(fiberOut.M)}`}&lt;br&gt;
cut-off wavelength λ&lt;sub&gt;c&lt;/sub&gt; = ${(1000*fiberOut.lc).toFixed(0)} nm&lt;br&gt;
${fiberOut.V &gt; 0.8 && fiberOut.V &lt; 2.6 ? `MFD (Marcuse) = ${fiberOut.mfd.toFixed(2)} µm · ` : ""}
step-index intermodal spread ≈ ${fiberOut.dtau.toFixed(1)} ns/km
&lt;/div&gt;`

3.3 Dispersion engineering, live (slides 76, 87–89)
\(D_w\) is negative and grows in magnitude when the core gets smaller and the index step larger. Pushing \(\lambda_0\) to 1550 nm gives a dispersion-shifted fiber (DSF). Stopping slightly before gives a non-zero DSF (NZ-DSF, G.655), which keeps a little dispersion to suppress four-wave mixing in WDM. The curves below were computed with the exact model above. Pick a core radius and a GeO\(_2\) concentration.







Show the Python
viewof aSel = Inputs.select(dgrid.radii, {value: 4.0, label: "core radius a (µm)", format: d =&gt; d.toFixed(2)})
viewof xSel = Inputs.select(dgrid.xs, {value: 0.035, label: "GeO₂ mole fraction", format: d =&gt; (100*d).toFixed(1) + " %"})


















Show the Python
